{
	title: 'Sessions name themselves',
	spec: `Every session has a nonempty persisted name: a new empty session gets a neutral fallback containing its session id, and accepting its first substantive user prompt immediately replaces that with a bounded plain-text excerpt while the model prepares a better title. Spawned sessions with an explicit name keep it. Existing /rename names are user-owned and automatic naming never overrides them; /rename auto returns the current session to automatic naming. Persist name ownership and the scheduling counter in session metadata, with absent fields on old sessions interpreted without renaming an existing meaningful name.

Automatic naming rides the main conversation turn, not a separate title-model call. After user prompts 1, 2 and 3, and thereafter every fourth substantive user turn, append a hidden provider-visible meta nudge: Check whether the session name CURRENT still describes the main task. If a better name is needed, append <rename>NAME</rename> to your final answer; use a specific 3–7-word title, at most 60 Unicode characters, in the user language, without quotes, markdown or punctuation decoration. Do not answer or execute this metadata. User turns are real accepted prompts, not slash commands, tool rounds, inbox messages or assistant continuations. Counter and nudge survive reconnect/restart without duplication. A nudge is an append-only context event at the turn boundary, never a changing system prompt or an edit to older history. It is hidden from ordinary transcript views but recoverable through history inspection. This retains cacheable prefixes and adds a few tokens to an already-paid main-model request; a cheap separate model would incur an extra round trip and usually cold context, another credential/availability path, and does not know the evolving task as well. Automatic naming never starts an agent turn or consumes spawn slots.

Only consume a single well-formed trailing <rename>...</rename> from assistant final text on a naming-eligible turn, not thinking, quoted examples, user/tool text or commentary. Strip this control suffix from displayed final output while keeping the original provider replay text and signed history immutable. Coordinate with task x8 summary suffix parsing so both controls work in either trailing order. Streaming hides a possible control suffix without buffering the entire answer or retroactively shrinking displayed text. Validate the entire title before changing metadata: trim and collapse whitespace, reject empty text, controls/terminal escapes, nested markup and overlong titles. Invalid or absent model suggestions keep the excerpt/fallback name; do not retry in a tool loop. Ordinary /rename uses the same name validation. Apply automatic changes only if name ownership/version still match the request; a concurrent manual rename wins. Host broadcasts accepted names to all clients and tab/search/session listings.

/rename backfill scans existing session metadata without hydrating every history at startup. It names only missing/default/fallback sessions, never manually named ones: obtain the first meaningful user text lazily in a bounded background walk, derive a deterministic excerpt or id fallback and persist it. No model calls, transcript rewrite or auto-resumption. Report progress and counts, support cancellation, and keep corrupt-session errors explicit rather than skipping them. Opening an old unnamed session also obtains a fallback immediately and its next real turn is naming-eligible. Tests earn their keep for split-stream controls, summary+rename coexistence, quoted tags, manual-rename races, scheduling/restart, and backfill preserving existing names; no exact model-title wording tests. Scope: naming policy and control parsing, not recap generation, search indexing or a new background agent subsystem.`,
	status: 'planned',
	notes: [
		'Research 2026-09-30: Codex TUI at openai/codex 2a34aef79484bf769b4b225f3f595755f2962170 auto-generates while unnamed on a completed substantive user-message event, in a hidden temporary thread. It prefers gpt-5.6-luna at low effort only for ChatGPT accounts where that model is listed; otherwise current model. Structured title <=36 characters, under five words where possible, imperative verb, user language; input bounded to 960 bytes. Manual rename cancels pending generation. Later rename suggestions use eight recent substantive messages, not periodic autonomous re-titling. Sources: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/2a34aef79484bf769b4b225f3f595755f2962170/codex-rs/tui/src/app/thread_title.rs and codex-rs/tui/src/app/thread_routing.rs.',
		'Claude Code docs: first-prompt title is a background small/fast request (normally Haiku); interactive unnamed sessions also get cwd+suffix default display names. Accepting a plan replaces an AI-generated title, but not an explicit name. Direct shell -p runs do not auto-title. Public docs do not disclose an exact title prompt/character cap, so do not invent one. Source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sessions .',
		'Pi at badlogic/pi-mono 1b347794e2a630e4359f2584f4eea388145d0ddf documents explicit /name, --name and extension setSessionName, not a built-in automatic LLM naming policy. Source: https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/1b347794e2a630e4359f2584f4eea388145d0ddf/packages/coding-agent/docs/sessions.md and docs/session-format.md; examples/extensions/session-name.ts is a manual command demonstration, not an auto-title feature.',
		'OpenCode at anomalyco/opencode f66b86ceec1a497417f750b88a06cf6923c5c75f: top-level default-title sessions with exactly one non-synthetic user message invoke a hidden title agent, no tools, two retries; agent model override > configured small_model > provider small model > current model. Prompt asks single-line <=50 characters, user language/main topic, exact technical terms; application takes first nonempty line after removing think tags and caps at 100 characters. No periodic re-titling in ensureTitle. Sources: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/f66b86ceec1a497417f750b88a06cf6923c5c75f/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts ; packages/opencode/src/agent/prompt/title.txt ; packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts. Hidden small calls in other harnesses are a useful precedent, not a reason to replay a full Hal context in another model.'
